# ShellCheck configuration — STUB.
#
# This file is a placeholder. It sets nothing, so ShellCheck behaves exactly as
# it does with no config at all: default severity, every check enabled.
#
# It exists so the repo has one obvious place to put shell-lint policy when
# someone decides what that policy is. Until then, an empty config is the
# honest state — it does not silence anything, and it does not claim a standard
# nobody has ruled on.
#
# Do not add `disable=` lines to make an existing script pass. That inverts what
# the file is for: it would turn a repo-wide standard into a per-annoyance
# escape hatch, and every later reader would inherit the exemption without the
# argument for it. Fix the script, or write the exemption where the offending
# line is (`# shellcheck disable=SCxxxx`) so it stays next to its reason.
#
# Syntax when this stops being a stub (one directive per line, no sections):
#   severity=warning
#   enable=require-variable-braces
#   disable=SC2154
#
# No shell script in this repo is linted by CI today. Adding a rule here does
# not create a gate; it only changes what a human or Codacy sees when they run
# ShellCheck by hand.
